# netsurf: fieldset and legend drawn as in a browser (patch 222)
# Generated 2026-10-07
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser 7fc3b8d (patch stack through 221)
#
# <legend> had no UA style, so it was an inline beside the fieldset's
# first control, inside a thin grey frame with 1.12em vertical margins:
# a form's sections looked nothing like a browser's.
#
#  - default.css: browsers' fieldset box (2px groove, padding 0.35em
#    0.75em 0.625em, 2px side margins, no vertical margin, min-width
#    min-content); legend a block of width fit-content with 2px side
#    padding, lifted onto the top border by a negative margin-top (the
#    border and padding) whose margin-bottom puts the padding back below
#    it -- the geometry browsers give it.
#  - box_construct.c, box.h: VB_LEGEND flags <legend> boxes.
#  - redraw.c: a block whose first in-flow child is a flagged legend
#    draws its borders d lower (the top border through the legend's
#    middle) in three clipped passes that leave the top border out
#    behind the legend.
#
# Test: testpages/pages/HTML-fieldset-legend.html (FIELDSET222, 5
# checks, Chromium 5/5; before, 1/5): the legend on the top border, the
# content 0.35em below it, the legend shrink-to-fit, the padding and
# border, and the margins.
